<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kameshwar Thakur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kameshwar Thakur was a Maithil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> of the Oinwar family who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithila">Mithila</a> from the Tughluq rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> after they overthrew the Karnat dynasty in 1324. Governing on their behalf, he founded the Oinwar dynasty, whose later kings, notably Shivasimha, patronised the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidyapati">Vidyapati</a>.</p></div>
